PhyCommander — licensing summary
================================

Copyright © 2014-2026 Angelo Leto <angelo@leto.blue>

This project is licensed under a set of complementary copyleft
licenses chosen to keep derivative works open. The boundaries below
are authoritative; each source file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier
that tracks them.


1. Network-facing software: AGPL-3.0-or-later
---------------------------------------------

The Rust streaming server and everything it serves over the network
is released under the **GNU Affero General Public License, version 3
or any later version** (see LICENSE-AGPL-3.0).

In scope:
  * physerver/src/**                          (binary + web + IPC + telemetry)
  * physerver/crates/phycmd-core/**            (protocol / transport / scheduler)
  * physerver/crates/phycmd-rust/**            (public Rust client crate)
  * physerver/crates/phycmd-py/**              (Python bindings)
  * physerver/static/**                        (dashboard HTML / JS / CSS / SVG
                                                assets that are NOT the project
                                                logo — see §6)

Practical effect: anyone who runs a modified PhyCommander server as a
network-available service must provide the corresponding source code
to the users interacting with it, as specified by AGPL §13. This is
the clause that prevents a third party from taking this codebase,
forking it privately, running it as SaaS, and giving nothing back.


2. Firmware, deployment plumbing, scripts: GPL-3.0-or-later
-----------------------------------------------------------

Everything that runs on the SAM3X8E or outside the server process is
released under the **GNU General Public License, version 3 or any
later version** (see LICENSE-GPL-3.0).

In scope:
  * ATSAM3X8E_FW/ATSAM3X8E_FW/src/**           (firmware, excluding the
                                                Atmel Software Framework
                                                bundled under src/ASF/ which
                                                retains its upstream
                                                permissive licenses, see §5)
  * scripts/**                                 (deployment, benchmarking,
                                                waveform utilities)
  * deploy/**                                  (systemd units, udev rules,
                                                policy-routing helpers)

Practical effect: binary distributions of the firmware or the scripts
must be accompanied by, or include an offer for, the corresponding
source code.


3. Hardware designs: CERN-OHL-S v2 (Strongly Reciprocal)
--------------------------------------------------------

Schematics, PCB layouts, mechanical CAD, and enclosure / front-panel
artwork are released under the **CERN Open Hardware Licence, version 2
— Strongly Reciprocal** (see LICENSE-CERN-OHL-S-2.0).

In scope:
  * companion_board/pcb/**                     (KiCad project for the
                                                passive Due shield
                                                backplane)
  * companion_board/panel_sketch/*.svg         (front / rear / backplane
                                                vectors)
  * docs/hardware/FrontPanel_2014.dwg          (original 2014 AutoCAD)
  * any future gerbers / BOMs / CAD under
    companion_board/ or docs/hardware/

Practical effect: modified hardware designs distributed to others
must be released under CERN-OHL-S as well, and the complete "Source"
(as defined by §1.11 of the licence) must be made available. This is
the natural copyleft analogue of AGPL for physical artefacts.


4. Narrative documentation and photos: CC-BY-SA-4.0
---------------------------------------------------

Long-form prose documentation, tutorials, README narrative, and
photographs of the physical device are released under the **Creative
Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International** licence (see
LICENSE-CC-BY-SA-4.0).

In scope:
  * README.md, CHANGELOG.md, SECURITY.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md,
    CONTRIBUTING.md
  * docs/** Markdown files (excluding docs/hardware/* which falls
    under §3)
  * phy_picts/**, docs/images/**               (photographs)


5. Third-party components
-------------------------

The Atmel Software Framework bundled in
`ATSAM3X8E_FW/ATSAM3X8E_FW/src/ASF/` is distributed under the
per-file Atmel (Microchip) permissive licences — see the header of
each ASF source. It is GPL-3.0-compatible and its inclusion in a
larger GPL-licensed firmware does not change its upstream terms.

Rust dependencies declared in `physerver/Cargo.toml` and
`physerver/crates/*/Cargo.toml` are upstream projects with their own
licences (overwhelmingly MIT, Apache-2.0, or both); see their
respective `LICENSE` files or `cargo-deny` / `cargo-about` output
for a complete inventory.


6. Trademarks and project identity
----------------------------------

The project name "PhyCommander" and its short form "PhyCMD", the
project logo (files `physerver/static/logo.svg` and
`physerver/static/logo-mark.svg`), and any distinctive visual
identity are **NOT** licensed under any of the licences above.

See TRADEMARKS.md for the full policy. Short version: forks must
rename before presenting themselves as the original project, and the
logo files cannot be reused except for unmodified attribution to
this project.


7. Contributions
----------------

Any contribution intentionally submitted for inclusion in this
project shall be licensed under the licence that applies to the
modified file (as defined by the boundaries above), without any
additional terms or conditions. Submitting a pull request constitutes
agreement to this. If a contribution spans files under different
licences, each hunk inherits the licence of the file it modifies.

If you need to contribute under a different arrangement (e.g. a
corporate CLA), contact the author before opening a pull request.


8. Attribution requirement on redistribution
--------------------------------------------

Keep this `LICENSE` file together with the applicable licence texts
(`LICENSE-AGPL-3.0`, `LICENSE-GPL-3.0`, `LICENSE-CERN-OHL-S-2.0`,
`LICENSE-CC-BY-SA-4.0`) and preserve the copyright line at the top
of this file. The per-file `SPDX-License-Identifier` headers must be
preserved on all source files they currently mark.
